RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
December 22, 2008
Due to the Christmas holiday season, the regular meeting of the Governing Body of the
City of Cheyenne was re-scheduled to begin at 3:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were:
MAYOR - Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr.
Collins, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Pierson, Mr. Segrave and Mr. Valdez. Absent: Dr. Rinne. The pledge
of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Bob Nicholas,
Acting City Attorney.
A PRESENTATION TO MAYOR JACK R. SPIKER FROM THE GEOGRAPHIC
INFORMATION SYSTEM EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE.  Joyce Pukash, Cheyenne/Laramie
County GIS Program, recognized Mayor Spiker for his support of the program and service as a
member of the executive committee, presented him with a Certificate of Appreciation plaque and
a historic map of the state of Wyoming.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Brown, and pursuant to
support received by Mr. Collins and Mr. Pierson, Mayor Spiker announced agenda item #21(a)
would be removed from the Consent Agenda.  Upon request by Mr. Collins, and pursuant to
support received by Mr. Brown and Mr. Segrave, Mayor Spiker announced agenda items #16
and 23(c) would also be removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mr. Collins moved to approve
remaining Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body present with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
DECEMBER 8, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
DECEMBER 15, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Valdez. Mr. Brown moved to divide the question to allow a separate vote on a voucher payable
to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Ms. Case requested a motion to
separate out the item be made instead of a motion to divide the question with Mayor Spiker
advising the motion, with the second, on the floor was to divide the question.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present with the exception of Ms. Case and
Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.  Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest) due to
the voucher payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, and vacated Council Chambers. Mr.
Collins moved to approve the voucher payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services ($345.90),
