CHANGE ORDERS/CONTRACT MODIFICATIONS:
Contract Modification No. 1 to Contract No. 5076 between the City of Cheyenne and
AVI Professional Corporation for additional design work and construction management services
for the Henderson Basin Flood Control Improvement Project (2007-2010 1% Sales Tax). Mr.
Segrave moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $450,635.00, seconded by Mr. Valdez.
Discussion followed and included the following topics: Project bid savings relative to estimated
engineer’s estimates, and services to be provided and costs (percentage) involved with the
proposed contract modification.  During discussion, Mayor Spiker ruled comments being made
pertaining to AVI’s work relationship with the City as out of order; not appropriate to the motion
on the floor.  During further comment involving contract criteria and past performance of AVI
involving City projects, Mr. Brown raised a point of order with Mayor Spiker ruling that
comments concerning previous performance could continue.  Ms. Case raised a point of order
regarding Mr. Brown’s lack of reference as to the reason he raised the point of order with Mayor
Spiker reviewing his previous ruling allowing discussion to continue.  Mr. Brown moved to
postpone for two weeks (to January 12, 2009) to allow for further research on costs involved in
the proposed modification, seconded by Mr. Pierson. During discussion on the motion to
postpone, Ms. Case raised a point of order noting language in Robert’s Rule of Order talks about
not speaking in the first person, and that Council members’ names or individual names should
not be used.  Discussion followed on the purpose of postponement, which is to provide further
review of percentage costs involved in the proposed modification relative to the engineer’s
estimate vs. the actual contract bid amount, and industry percentage standards. Motion to
postpone for two weeks carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
[CA]
Contract Modification No. 2 to Contract No. 5280 between the City of Cheyenne and
Reiman Corporation to clarify warranty responsibilities on the Norris Viaduct Project (1%
Specific Purpose Sales and Use Tax) -- referred to Finance Committee.
